WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.433 --> 00:00:02.767
We all should be aware
of every single person

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:05.600
who dies fighting for
our freedom and democracy

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.300
around the world.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.533
Where we're going, Sadr
City, over two million people

00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:15.633
lived under a dictator's
boot for 24 years.

00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:17.467
And we can build a
better future for them,

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:18.400
for the whole country.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.200
That's why we're going.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.233
You know, we all live
pretty comfortable lives.

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:26.900
We hear things on the
news, and especially

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.667
nowadays, when
it's such a sort of

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.667
swipe-able, switch-able world.

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:33.133
So now, more than ever, I
think, it's important to tell

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.600
these stories.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.433
OK, well--

00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:36.233
I love you.

00:00:36.233 --> 00:00:38.533
I love you.

00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:40.834
See you.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:44.600
I think everybody on
this set, actor-wise,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.200
has approached their roles
with a huge level of humility.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.633
And just going, I'm here
in service of the story.

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:56.166
I'm here in service of
these men and women.

00:01:00.166 --> 00:01:01.367
We have Comanche Six.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.500
Find a secure defensive position
and wait for extraction.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.300
We're coming.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.300
War affects everyone.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.900
You know, war affects
US soldiers that

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.834
are there, in the trenches.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.567
It affects their spouses.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:14.000
It affects their children.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.433
And that is what
is so important.

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:18.166
I really think is that,
it's not just the soldiers.

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.533
It's not just the
military who goes to war.

00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:23.066
We all go to war.

00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:24.333
Are you sure
you're not worried?

00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:28.367
There is one incident in
the entire city last year.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.266
We're not even bringing
the heavy armor.

00:01:30.266 --> 00:01:31.633
If there was a gun
going off over there,

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:34.533
it's probably just some fools
celebrating a Cowboys game.

00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:37.000
Well, it never hurts
to be extra sure.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.567
I hope what
audiences take away

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:43.967
from this series
is that these are

00:01:43.967 --> 00:01:47.066
your soldiers, your families.

00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:50.700
This didn't just
happen that one time.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.600
It still happens.

